  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For the mission to count as successful, do the two destroyed key parts have to be destroyed by the same aircraft in a single sortie, or is it enough that across the whole mission (possibly multiple sorties) at least two of the four parts end up destroyed?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the specific conditions for mission success (single sortie vs. cumulative), which constitutes one independent semantic query."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is the mission carried out by a single aircraft that makes multiple sorties (each sortie being one round trip to one target part, dropping all bombs it carries on that part), or by multiple aircraft each making one sortie?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response presents a single binary choice regarding the mission structure (single aircraft with multiple sorties vs. multiple aircraft with one sortie each), which constitutes one semantically independent clarification question."
}

